{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtIII"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtIII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Three fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(≈ 698.045 cents). Six fifths — A→E, B→F♯, F♯→C♯, C♯→A♭, E♭→B♭, B♭→F — are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma (≈ 700.000 cents). The remaining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"three fifths — E→B, A♭→E♭, F→C — are pure. The circle closes exactly:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"3×(1\/6) + 6×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}]},{"text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Differs from ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtII","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only in the placement of the sixth-comma group on the flat side: E♭→B♭ is tempered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"here where it is pure in Neidhardt II, and F→C is pure here where it is tempered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Neidhardt II."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/neidhardtiii"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtIII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"title":"neidhardtIII","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE12neidhardtIIIAEvpZ","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","roleHeading":"Type Property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"symbolKind":"property","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"WellTemperament","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of